# `xrandr --output HEADLESS-1 --dryrun --mode 800x600`, measured 2026-09-10 on
# sway + Xwayland (scratchpad/b7/cap1.log connection 9, requests 19-20).
# `--dryrun` still grabs: `grab_server` is a separate flag defaulting true and
# cleared only by --nograb [xrandr.c:55, 2723]. So an EMPTY grab is a real
# batch that must commit nothing -- a proxy that read it as "apply what is
# there" would make --dryrun the one flag that changes the screen.
